 ## Overview
-This method calculates the ray origin in volume texture space for a given vertex on the near plane quad, used for testing ray casting shaders [S1, unofficial]. It transforms a vertex from view space to world space and then maps it into the local volume coordinate system [S1, unofficial]. It differs from camera-space ray setup [4179-object-space-ray-setup-camera-space-transformation-for-ray-o.md] by operating directly on object-space vertices and using hardware interpolation of 3D UVs, rather than computing ray origins and directions in camera space [G].
+This method calculates the ray origin in volume texture space for a given vertex on the near plane quad, used for testing ray casting shaders [S1, unofficial]. It transforms a vertex from view space to world space using the inverse model-view matrix, then translates and scales it into the local volume coordinate system [S1, unofficial]. It differs from camera-space ray setup [4179-object-space-ray-setup-camera-space-transformation-for-ray-o.md] by operating directly on object-space vertices and using hardware interpolation of 3D UVs, rather than computing ray origins and directions in camera space [G].
 
